THEMES = [
 "**Agents are moving to always-on, cloud-hosted teammates.** Google's Gemini agent (one agent across Docs, mobile, and CLI, with 'dream mode' reflection) and ChatGPT dots on mobile both separate the chat window from where the agent runs, so multi-hour tasks survive a closed laptop and you can approve them from your phone.",
 "**Cost discipline is now an engineering topic.** OpenAI's DevDay talk says to measure cost per task, not per token, and covers caching, programmatic tool calling, and reasoning effort. Google is adding hard spend caps with smart routing, and GitHub's HydraFusion plus local-model routing pushes simple work to free on-device models.",
 "**Local AI hardware is a big deal, and RAM prices are hurting.** 128–160 GB unified-memory mini PCs (GMKtec EVO-X3), DGX Station and RTX Pro 6000 rigs running a smart orchestrator with cheap local workers, Gemma 4 and EmbeddingGemma 2 on-device, and Jeff Geerling on SBC prices and shortages.",
 "**Context files and skills are becoming the standard way to steer agents.** AGENTS.md, DESIGN.md, and SKILL.md (keep AGENTS.md about 12 lines), Looker skills plus MCP, and Boundary's pipeline that turns team session history into durable agent memory.",
 "**Guardrails for agents that take actions.** Require human confirmation for irreversible browser actions (enforced server-side), give agents their own identity and audit trail, scope service accounts and MCP tools narrowly, and on the ops side use agent-assisted incident triage (Elastic and Harness).",
]
